      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a structured quick-start guide for the NX-5 Proximity Sensor designed to pass your QC tool's automation rules while remaining clear and functional for engineers.\n\n# NX-5 Proximity Sensor Quick-Start Guide\n\n## Safety Requirements\nBefore installation, ensure the environment is dry and the ambient temperature remains below 60°C. Do not expose the sensor to any liquids.\n\n## Installation\n1. Place the component in a standard 4-pin I2C location.\n2. Connect VCC to Pin 1, GND to Pin 2, SDA to Pin 3, and SCL to Pin 4.\n3. Verify all connections are secure before powering the system.\n\n## Calibration Procedure\n1. Power on the sensor using the regulated 5V DC supply.\n2. Hold the reset button down for exactly 3 seconds while it is ON.\n3. Release the button to confirm the sensor is calibrated.\n\n## Electrical Specifications\n*   **Voltage:** 5V DC (strictly regulated required).\n*   **Interface:** I2C protocol.\n\n## Troubleshooting\nIf the sensor fails to initialize, re-check the pinout sequence and ensure the reset hold time",
